'''Happosai''' is a [[:Category:Super Rare Cats|Super Rare Cat]] that can be unlocked by playing the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the [[Ranma 1/2 Collaboration Event]]. He was added in [[Version 10.4 Update|Version 10.4]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 601
|rarity = SR
|name1 = Happosai
|name2 = Happosai (Lewd)
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Happosai (Lewd)''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Like the anime character he depicts, Happosai is an unconventional unit with some knacks. His stats are most similar to [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Ring Girl Cat]], though his most notable strengths over her are in damage and speed, meaning he can serve as a serviceable attacker before the acquisition of Pizza Cat and his [[Talents]]. Happosai's actual selling point, however, is his [[Knockback]] ability against three whole traits. Red, Floating, and Zombie contain a variety of enemies Happosai can defend against, such as [[Bore]], [[Teacher Bun Bun]] and his variants, [[Zir Zeal]], [[Zang Roo]], and (with mixed results) [[Lord Gravey]]. His trait flexibility can occasionally give him an edge over other crowd controllers if multiple of his targets are present in a stage as well as the general advantage of [[Area Attack]] and a good proc chance. His unusually high speed can help with quickly getting into action, though it may get him in a sticky situation if he clips into an enemy. While the three traits he counters already have a wealth of respectable crowd-control options, Happosai manages to work well as a pusher that does its job when other units might not cut it.

{{Job|Classification = Crowd-Controller & Rusher}}

